{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Migration Reminder on Schema Change",
  "description": "When backend/src/db/schema.ts is edited, reminds the agent to generate a migration, review the SQL, create a migration test, and update backup/restore if a new table was added.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "backend/src/db/schema.ts"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "The database schema was modified. Follow the Database Migration SOP:\n\n1. Run `bun run db:generate` from the backend/ directory to generate a migration.\n2. Review the generated SQL file in backend/drizzle/ to confirm it matches your intent. Watch for unintended DROP TABLE operations.\n3. Stage all three generated artifacts: `backend/drizzle/000N_*.sql`, `backend/drizzle/meta/000N_snapshot.json`, and the new `backend/drizzle/meta/_journal.json` entry. Without the snapshot the next `db:generate` re-emits this migration's DDL.\n4. Create a migration test file `backend/src/db/__tests__/migration-000N.test.ts` following the pattern in DatabaseMigrations.md steering. `migration-general.test.ts` needs no edit — it derives the expected table list from schema.ts — but it does fail if that per-migration file is missing.\n5. If a new table was added, update `TABLE_SCHEMA_MAP` and `TABLE_FILENAME_MAP` in `backend/src/config.ts`, and update backup/restore files.\n6. Run the migration tests: `bun test src/db/__tests__/migration-general.test.ts src/db/__tests__/migration-000N.test.ts`\n\nDo not skip any of these steps."
  }
}